<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen narrowly traded pre-weekend.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen narrowly traded pre-weekend.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 8.30 a.m./2230 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	   2669.70  +23.30   DJIA  cl	8020.77  -18.11</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl	 2700	+8   US 30yr cl	 6.49   +0.01</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    93.415  -0.045   Gold NY 323.75 Lon fix 319.40</p>
<p>AUD	   0.7351 (Thu 0.7368)   CRB Index cl   234.19   +0.17</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20519.25 +160.51   FTSE cl	 4949.0x  -15.20</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   935.30   -2.65   NZSE40	  2493.49   -1.17</p>
<p>--------------------------(July 18)----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks seen mixed, eyes on next week's key inflation data. &quot;We had a good day yesterday. You might see it a bit quieter today ahead of the weekend,&quot; said a Sydney-based broker.  </p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$18.42 (-.04), A$19.22 (-.04), A$6.33 (-.01), A$7.68 (+.02)</p>
<p>*Wall Street paused on its record shattering run, pulling blue chips lower. Nasdaq posted its first loss in two weeks.</p>
<p>*ADRs: News Corp 18-7/16 (+2/16), BHP 27-5/8 (+9/16), WMC 22-3/4 (+1/16), National Australia Bank 71-7/16 (+5/16)</p>
<p>*Gold price was higher. On LME, copper made steady upside progress after an early dip to five months lows while the rest of the complex was mainly firmer.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
